WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.070
Visitors began climbing
Uluru in the late 1930s.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.470
In 1964, a chain was installed.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.250
On 26 October 2019, the
climb closed for good.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.310
Yet the park remains open.

5
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.530
Why close one of Australia's
most famous attractions?

6
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.870
Only for safety?

7
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.730
Because the rock was eroding?

8
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.010
In this mission, you'll
follow tourists to Antarctica,

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.550
now over 100,000 a year, and
the rules that limit landings.

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.930
Then you'll face the heat
at Uluru: at nearby Yulara,

11
00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:37.370
the January mean maximum
is 38.6 degrees Celsius.

12
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.550
Your mission: explain
why Uluru's climb closed,

13
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.760
while the park remains open.
